499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (Last summer I was in Barcelona at the Padel World Summit, the largest padel trade fair in the world. I have been running CoolPadel for a while, a business of tennis, padel, and pickleball keychains for clubs and brands, and as a padel enthusiast, I could not miss the opportunity)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (During the event, I spoke with 116 of the 120 stands that were there, and with many other attendees who told me how they saw the industry. Additionally, this March I have been at RacquetX and at the Miami Premier Padel and I have been able to see the state of the North American market)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 448 0 R
/E (In general terms, I believe that padel as a business is a present opportunity with a lot of future. Even so, this by no means implies that everything is as attractive as it sometimes seems. Hype is a common companion and one must be careful. Without a doubt, the key lies in the solid base of amateur players that does not stop growing)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
